WEBVTT

00:20.590 --> 00:24.070
You've brilliantly fallen into my trap, Sunred.

00:24.570 --> 00:28.910
With the sun shrouded by darkness, your powers are useless.

00:28.910 --> 00:30.430
You're no different than a puny civilian.

00:31.030 --> 00:33.630
My corona keeps burning

00:33.630 --> 00:35.370
even when the sun cannot be seen!

00:35.590 --> 00:37.120
Nonsense.

00:37.120 --> 00:38.670
Hell Scissors!

00:48.090 --> 00:49.670
Sunred,

00:49.670 --> 00:52.730
I've sliced you in half along with the Fortress of Darkness.

00:52.730 --> 00:55.160
I'm still alive, Hengel!

00:59.100 --> 01:01.540
Sunred Ultimate Form,

01:01.540 --> 01:03.260
Firebird Form!

01:04.850 --> 01:06.500
The Firebird Form

01:06.500 --> 01:10.310
is the Sun Fighter's ultimate form

01:10.310 --> 01:13.030
which is activated when Sunred's Corona Energy reaches full power.

01:14.060 --> 01:16.170
Persistent bastard.

01:16.670 --> 01:19.880
Time for you to go back to hell, Hengel!

01:19.880 --> 01:23.090
Firebird Attack!

01:24.540 --> 01:26.880
Hell Scissors!

01:45.940 --> 01:48.100
General Hengel.

01:48.100 --> 01:49.770
You were quite a fearsome opponent.

02:00.760 --> 02:04.870
You've done well to come this far, Sunred.

02:04.870 --> 02:06.240
General Vamp!

02:06.240 --> 02:07.540
This is the real you?

02:07.540 --> 02:09.020
Sunred,

02:09.020 --> 02:12.690
many sacrifices have been made in order to bring you down.

02:13.390 --> 02:18.040
Now join me, my cute monsters,

02:18.040 --> 02:20.300
it all ends today!

02:20.300 --> 02:23.080
Now come, Sunred!

02:26.860 --> 02:28.800
Vamp!

02:28.800 --> 02:31.200
Sunred!

02:36.880 --> 02:39.860
That was wonderful.

02:49.490 --> 02:52.290
Death Lance!

02:52.870 --> 02:54.260
Why you...

02:54.260 --> 02:56.970
Tiger Crush!

02:58.610 --> 02:59.190
That was close!

02:59.190 --> 03:00.450
Like hell it was!

03:02.410 --> 03:04.350
Enough is freakin' enough.

03:04.350 --> 03:08.340
How dare you attack me when I'm busy with the end of year.

03:08.790 --> 03:11.340
You were <i>busy </i>, Mr. Red?

03:11.340 --> 03:12.440
No way.

03:12.440 --> 03:14.670
I think you called his bluff, Master Vamp.

03:14.670 --> 03:17.620
Right? Thank goodness.

03:19.020 --> 03:21.740
What are you laughing at?

03:21.740 --> 03:24.510
I really have to be somewhere in a little bit.

03:25.260 --> 03:26.670
Seriously?

03:26.870 --> 03:29.570
Stop acting so surprised about everything!

03:29.570 --> 03:30.280
Um...

03:30.280 --> 03:31.080
What?

03:31.080 --> 03:34.110
Could we stop sitting up straight, then?

03:34.110 --> 03:36.270
You cocky son of a bitch!

03:36.270 --> 03:38.130
You need to quit bitching

03:38.130 --> 03:40.830
and reflect on what you've done harder than all these punks!

03:40.830 --> 03:43.380
I think that's enough, Mr. Red.

03:44.250 --> 03:45.790
A one, two:

03:45.790 --> 03:47.870
Thank you for the lecture!

03:47.870 --> 03:49.370
Fix that bench, okay?

03:49.770 --> 03:50.290
Yes, sir!

03:51.860 --> 03:53.680
I didn't think he'd ever leave.

03:53.680 --> 03:56.720
Yeah, today was tiring as usual.

03:57.020 --> 03:58.830
Thanks for the hard work, you guys.

03:58.830 --> 04:00.680
Thank you for the hard work!

04:00.680 --> 04:02.030
I'm hungry now.

04:02.030 --> 04:03.940
I'm starving too!

04:03.940 --> 04:07.080
Why don't we all go out to eat then?

04:07.080 --> 04:08.640
All right!

04:08.640 --> 04:11.480
Come on now, fix that bench first.

04:11.480 --> 04:12.610
Okay.

04:32.150 --> 04:33.420
Come on in!

04:36.150 --> 04:38.150
What should we order, Master Vamp?

04:38.150 --> 04:40.150
Just get whatever you guys want.

04:40.150 --> 04:43.120
The food here's both cheap and delicious, so there's no need to hold back.

04:43.120 --> 04:43.700
Yes, sir.

04:43.700 --> 04:46.210
I want a medium beer, glug glug.

04:46.800 --> 04:47.720
Excuse me?

04:47.720 --> 04:48.290
Yes?

04:48.290 --> 04:51.430
Can we get five draft beers and two sour plum pickled cucumbers?

04:51.430 --> 04:53.400
Your brain's made of crab guts!

04:53.400 --> 04:55.600
And can we get two boiled crab guts?

04:55.600 --> 04:58.810
Oh their skewered chicken meatballs and boiled tendons are awesome too.

04:58.810 --> 04:59.760
Let's get those as well.

04:59.760 --> 05:00.540
Yes, sir.

05:00.540 --> 05:01.960
Number Two?

05:01.960 --> 05:02.680
Let's see.

05:02.680 --> 05:06.380
Can we get three skewered chicken meatballs and two boiled tendons?

05:06.380 --> 05:08.150
And three skewer sets please.

05:08.150 --> 05:09.440
We'll just order these for now.

05:09.440 --> 05:11.430
For now!

05:11.430 --> 05:13.730
Didn't you just get up a few moments ago, Tiser?

05:13.730 --> 05:15.130
Are you sure you can drink beer right now?

05:15.130 --> 05:16.920
Easy, easy.

05:19.480 --> 05:21.960
So I don't know what to do.

05:21.960 --> 05:23.670
Maybe I'm just too tired lately.

05:23.000 --> 05:23.970
Look, it's Kayoko!

05:23.970 --> 05:25.170
You're right.

05:25.170 --> 05:26.420
Kayoko!

05:26.420 --> 05:29.310
Maybe I should just break up with him.

05:31.990 --> 05:33.130
Can you believe it?

05:33.130 --> 05:36.080
He was still sleeping when I came back from work yesterday.

05:36.080 --> 05:38.470
He could have at least cleaned up the apartment.

05:39.840 --> 05:41.020
Now that I think about it,

05:41.020 --> 05:43.980
he woke up even earlier than me this morning and asked for money.

05:43.980 --> 05:46.540
That idiot's probably been playing pachinko all day since morning.

05:47.840 --> 05:49.580
You know,

05:49.580 --> 05:51.900
he's exactly what they'd call <i>that </i>.

05:51.900 --> 05:52.920
<i>That </i>?

05:52.920 --> 05:55.290
Yeah, <i>that </i>.

05:55.290 --> 05:57.120
I mean you're the breadwinner, right?

05:58.120 --> 05:58.950
Yeah.

06:00.760 --> 06:04.810
We already ordered, didn't we?

06:04.810 --> 06:05.660
Yes.

06:05.660 --> 06:08.210
Here you go, five beers.

06:06.960 --> 06:08.610
Easy, easy.

06:08.610 --> 06:09.900
So yeah,

06:09.900 --> 06:11.800
it's like I keep telling you:

06:11.800 --> 06:13.590
Just break up with him already.

06:13.820 --> 06:15.940
There's no future in that guy.

06:17.250 --> 06:20.280
You're almost thirty now, right?

06:20.280 --> 06:21.350
Yeah.

06:22.740 --> 06:24.570
What are you going to do about marriage?

06:26.490 --> 06:28.840
Are you going to marry <i>that guy </i>?

06:31.540 --> 06:33.080
Kayoko...

06:34.940 --> 06:36.380
I don't know.

06:36.980 --> 06:38.930
I just don't know anymore.

06:39.650 --> 06:41.320
Kayoko!

06:41.520 --> 06:43.160
He's got no job,

06:43.160 --> 06:44.830
and he doesn't help out with the housework.

06:44.830 --> 06:46.370
He doesn't even socialize.

06:46.370 --> 06:47.990
His personality...

06:49.230 --> 06:50.870
I can't say that it's great.

06:50.870 --> 06:52.940
He's useless, I tell you.

06:52.940 --> 06:55.500
He's a shining example of someone who's unfit for society.

06:55.500 --> 06:56.690
Nothing but trash, I say.

06:56.690 --> 06:57.510
But...

06:57.510 --> 06:59.050
You're better off without him.

06:59.050 --> 07:00.030
Still...

07:00.430 --> 07:05.440
He may be unfit for society, but he's the one who's protecting it.

07:07.130 --> 07:10.920
No one's exactly <i>asking </i> your boyfriend to do it, you know.

07:09.840 --> 07:12.010
But it's not like he has a choice.

07:13.950 --> 07:16.540
He <i>is </i> a Hero, you know.

07:16.540 --> 07:17.820
Kayoko...

07:18.020 --> 07:20.020
Can I get a dontakatan on the rocks here?

07:18.920 --> 07:20.020
I'm thinking,

07:20.020 --> 07:23.210
maybe you're the one who's making him useless.

07:23.620 --> 07:25.180
If you break up with him,

07:25.180 --> 07:27.040
he has no choice but to quit being a Hero

07:27.040 --> 07:29.240
and get himself a job.

07:29.240 --> 07:30.590
Think about it, it'll be good for him too.

07:30.590 --> 07:32.870
A dontakatan on the rocks.

07:34.760 --> 07:36.640
Quit?

07:37.710 --> 07:39.830
How could he possibly quit?

07:39.830 --> 07:43.250
He has the blood of a Hero flowing inside of him, you know.

07:48.910 --> 07:49.640
Hold on a—

07:49.640 --> 07:53.140
How could you be so judgmental when you don't know anything about him?

07:53.140 --> 07:54.440
He's got no job, you say?

07:54.440 --> 07:57.350
His job is to protect the world!

07:57.350 --> 07:59.870
The reason why he doesn't help with housework or socialize,

07:59.870 --> 08:03.690
is because he's disappointed that there's no longer a place for Heroes like him in this world.

08:04.360 --> 08:06.020
Um, hello?

08:06.020 --> 08:09.220
You're the one who asked me to hear you out, remember?

08:09.220 --> 08:10.820
What do you want me to do exactly?

08:10.820 --> 08:11.850
Well, I—

08:11.850 --> 08:15.120
Mr. Red is a nice and kind person!

08:15.120 --> 08:16.980
Vamp!

08:16.980 --> 08:17.770
Who's this?

08:17.770 --> 08:20.510
There's nothing wrong with Mr. Red's personality.

08:21.150 --> 08:24.270
No matter how many times we fail at killing him,

08:24.270 --> 08:27.500
he still bothers to fight us time after time even while insulting us for it.

08:27.500 --> 08:28.700
That's right.

08:28.700 --> 08:30.840
He always gives 100 percent

08:30.840 --> 08:33.230
even when he's fighting monsters like us.

08:33.230 --> 08:35.380
His dedication almost breaks my heart.

08:35.380 --> 08:38.870
I actually think his insults are his way of encouraging us to do better.

08:39.010 --> 08:40.110
Yeah.

08:40.110 --> 08:44.070
It really makes us want to nab him for good the next time around, right?

08:44.170 --> 08:47.480
One time I was so angry about losing to him that I couldn't sleep.

08:47.480 --> 08:48.800
Me too!

08:48.800 --> 08:50.140
Me three!

08:50.990 --> 08:52.660
Kayoko.

08:54.800 --> 08:56.620
Mr. Red really needs you.

08:56.620 --> 08:58.260
Mr. Red really needs you.

08:59.990 --> 09:04.100
You mean the world to him,

09:04.100 --> 09:06.870
so don't say you're breaking up with him, okay?

09:32.110 --> 09:35.390
Why not have a drink at Izakaya Iida today?

09:39.770 --> 09:40.660
Hey!

09:42.320 --> 09:43.180
Kayoko!

09:43.180 --> 09:44.570
What are you—

09:45.020 --> 09:47.070
Why are you dressed like that?

09:48.510 --> 09:50.930
I bought it with the money you gave me.

09:52.150 --> 09:54.610
I was kinda bored,

09:54.610 --> 09:57.710
so I figured I'd send in my résumé to this company that was hiring.

09:58.210 --> 10:01.730
They told me to come in for an interview today,

10:01.730 --> 10:02.950
so I went.

10:09.290 --> 10:13.460
But I didn't get the job.

10:14.980 --> 10:16.020
Sorry.

10:21.190 --> 10:22.450
You're silly.

10:27.040 --> 10:29.030
If you were busy...

10:30.570 --> 10:32.300
If a Hero like you were busy,

10:32.300 --> 10:34.920
who would the world turn to for help?

10:40.580 --> 10:41.790
Say...

10:41.790 --> 10:42.370
Yeah?

10:43.310 --> 10:47.080
Tomorrow's Christmas Eve, right?

10:47.080 --> 10:48.450
Yup.

10:48.450 --> 10:49.880
I see.

10:50.480 --> 10:53.540
So, which company did you apply to?

10:53.540 --> 10:54.720
Does it really matter?

10:54.720 --> 10:55.930
Tell me!

10:55.930 --> 10:56.780
Shut up!

11:02.140 --> 11:05.230
Didn't I tell you to go buy a cake?

11:05.230 --> 11:07.370
What possessed you to blow all the money on pachinko?

11:07.370 --> 11:08.300
W-Well,

11:08.300 --> 11:11.500
the pachinko place said that they had presents for us, so...

11:11.500 --> 11:13.620
You really think they'd have presents?

11:13.620 --> 11:16.770
It's no big deal; I can always buy you cake some other time, you know.

11:16.770 --> 11:19.430
And how do you plan on doing that, Mr. Unfit for Society!

11:22.400 --> 11:25.320
You make such a cute ornament, Usacots.

11:25.320 --> 11:27.810
I'm not a Christmas ornament!

11:27.810 --> 11:28.660
Usa!

11:29.260 --> 11:31.380
I kill youz!

11:31.380 --> 11:33.190
Hey, Turtle Boy!

11:33.190 --> 11:33.780
Yes?

11:33.780 --> 11:36.410
We haven't had a party like this since the group date, huh?

11:36.410 --> 11:38.060
I guess not.

11:38.060 --> 11:39.220
Come on, you guys!

11:39.220 --> 11:41.150
Less talk, more work!

11:41.150 --> 11:42.000
More work!

11:42.000 --> 11:43.380
What about you?

11:43.540 --> 11:44.950
Thanks for the hard work you guys!

11:44.950 --> 11:46.350
Thank you!

11:46.350 --> 11:48.520
What took you so long, Has-been Killer!

11:48.520 --> 11:49.970
Oh shut up.

11:49.970 --> 11:52.910
We didn't want to rush picking everyone's presents you know.

11:52.910 --> 11:56.120
"Picking" everyone's presents, my ass.

11:56.120 --> 11:58.240
Knowing you, you probably just got a bunch of stupid junk nobody wants.

11:58.240 --> 12:00.180
You better watch your damn mouth, bro.

12:00.180 --> 12:02.860
You're brothers so stop fighting!

12:02.860 --> 12:04.650
I don't think they can, though.

12:05.320 --> 12:07.920
Thank you for the hard work, Mr. Usa!

12:07.920 --> 12:09.030
Same to you guys.

12:09.030 --> 12:10.210
Easy, easy.

12:11.800 --> 12:13.110
All right, it's ready.

12:13.500 --> 12:16.700
Call Mr. Red and Kayoko for me, Geirus.

12:16.700 --> 12:18.290
Right away, sir!

12:18.920 --> 12:21.960
I hope they like the cake.

12:22.760 --> 12:24.690
Astro Fighter Sunred.

12:24.690 --> 12:27.910
This is the magnificent story of the conflict between good and evil

12:27.910 --> 12:31.450
that takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

12:40.520 --> 12:44.590
FIN
